    cross_references: [],
    fullText: "MEMORANDUM CIRCULAR\nNO. 06-04-99\n\nSUBJECT: QUALIFICATIONS AND NUMBER OF RADIO PERSONNEL REQUIRED ON-BOARD PHILIPPINES REGISTERED GMDSS VESSELS.\n\nIn view of the mandatory full compliance to the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System (GMDSS) effective February 01, 1999 as required by the Radio Regulations, the following minimum qualification and number of radio personnel on board Philippine registered vessels are hereby required:\n\n1. Two deck Certificate officers (who is not the master) with General Operator Certificate (GOC) or one exclusive radio officer with both GOC and Radio Electronic Certificate (REC).\n\n2. For ships with At-Sea (on-board) maintenance capability, two deck officers with GOC who is not the master and one non-exclusive radio officer holding both GOC and REC.\n\nThis Circular shall take effect immediately.\n\nApril 12, 1999, Quezon City, Philippines.\n\n(SGD.) JOSEPH A. SANTIAGO\nCommissioner\n\n(SGD.) NESTOR C. DACANAY          (SGD.) AURELIO M. UMALI\nDeputy Commissioner               Deputy Commissioner",
    sections: [
      {
        heading: "Required Qualifications and Personnel",
        body: "Issued for mandatory compliance with the Global Maritime Distress and Safety System (GMDSS), effective February 1, 1999. Philippine-registered vessels must carry either: two deck certificate officers (not the master) with General Operator Certificate (GOC), or one exclusive radio officer with both GOC and Radio Electronic Certificate (REC); or for ships with at-sea maintenance capability, two GOC-holding deck officers plus one non-exclusive radio officer holding both GOC and REC."
      },
      {
        heading: "Effectivity",
        body: "Took effect immediately upon issuance, April 12, 1999, Quezon City, by Commissioner Joseph A. Santiago."
      }
    ]
